+Feature: DOM node identity
+  As a user interacting with the todo list
+  I want DOM nodes to be preserved across state changes
+  So that the interface remains stable during rapid interactions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggling a todo preserves sibling DOM nodes
+
+    Scenario: Checking a todo leaves other todos intact
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then both todos are visible
+      And the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" does not have the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking a todo leaves other todos intact
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | true      |
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then both todos are visible
+      And the todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Toggling preserves all three todos in the list
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+        | Clean house  | false     |
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Walk the dog"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class
+      And the todo "Clean house" does not have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all preserves DOM node identity
+
+    Scenario: Marking all complete preserves the list
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then both todos are visible
+      And all todos are completed
+
+    Scenario: Unmarking all preserves the list
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | true      |
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then both todos are visible
+      And all todos are active
+
+    Scenario: Multiple rapid toggles do not corrupt the list
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then both todos are visible
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then both todos are visible
+      And all todos are active
+
+  Rule: Routing preserves visible todos
+
+    Scenario: Back button after filtering shows the correct todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | true      |
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then only the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then only the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then both todos are visible
